1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,340
[SITARA] But this must be
the moment

2
00:00:02,470 --> 00:00:03,590
I've been waiting for.

3
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:05,220
[gasps] How so?

4
00:00:05,340 --> 00:00:07,430
What could we hope
to accomplish?

5
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:09,100
I have great knowledge.

6
00:00:09,470 --> 00:00:10,560
If you'll allow,

7
00:00:10,810 --> 00:00:13,020
I'll serve you as your
new Jada stone, Highness.

8
00:00:13,140 --> 00:00:16,150
Please, just lend me your power.

9
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:21,700
And the two of us
can summon a fierce storm.

10
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:23,740
[insects trilling]

11
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:29,120
[Sitara sighs softly]

12
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:32,660
What have I done?
Not only did I ignore

13
00:00:32,790 --> 00:00:35,170
Princess Sorghaghtani's
orders...

14
00:00:35,290 --> 00:00:37,460
[gasps softly] Hold on,

15
00:00:37,590 --> 00:00:39,170
I'm not...

16
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:40,630
♪

17
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:43,010
[gasps]

18
00:00:44,590 --> 00:00:47,220
I'm not her slave, am I?

19
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:52,310
Ah, there you are. Fatima!

20
00:00:53,060 --> 00:00:55,650
[SITARA] Lady Töregene
and I have suffered greatly,

21
00:00:55,770 --> 00:00:58,150
but she's been forced
to bear her pain

22
00:00:58,270 --> 00:00:59,570
far longer than mine.

23
00:00:59,690 --> 00:01:01,150
-[SHIRA] Hey.
-Which is why...

24
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:04,070
Tell this
to Princess Sorghaghtani.

25
00:01:04,190 --> 00:01:05,320
I've found my way

26
00:01:05,410 --> 00:01:07,700
into a much more
convenient position out here.

27
00:01:07,820 --> 00:01:10,030
Uh, is that right?

28
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:12,290
Well, all the better then.

29
00:01:14,710 --> 00:01:16,210
[SITARA] No need to worry.

30
00:01:16,330 --> 00:01:19,960
I understand now.
I know what I must do.

31
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,420
[Shira exhales]

32
00:01:24,510 --> 00:01:28,800
[SITARA]
So just you wait, Mongols.

33
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:30,640
♪

34
00:01:33,850 --> 00:01:37,940
[♪ opening theme song playing]

35
00:03:13,030 --> 00:03:14,700
[groans] Uh?

36
00:03:14,830 --> 00:03:16,080
♪

37
00:03:19,870 --> 00:03:22,540
Uh, what's all this, Chagatai?

38
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:25,880
[Ögedei groans]

39
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,210
I offer you
my deepest apologies.

40
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:31,260
[ÖGEDEI AND ILÜGE] Huh?

41
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:34,300
First, I challenged
the Great Kha'an to a wager.

42
00:03:34,430 --> 00:03:37,510
Then I displayed the utmost
insolence by actually winning.

43
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:39,060
Oh, you mean that?

44
00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:41,640
[ÖGEDEI] Oh...

45
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:43,480
For this grave offense,

46
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:44,980
I am prepared to be flogged

47
00:03:45,110 --> 00:03:47,030
or even to receive
a death sentence.

48
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:49,070
Please do with me as you will.

49
00:03:49,690 --> 00:03:50,780
Hm?

50
00:03:52,030 --> 00:03:54,740
[chuckles] You are forgiven,
my brother.

51
00:03:54,870 --> 00:03:57,240
You know
I am not angered so easily.

52
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,450
Uh?

53
00:04:01,410 --> 00:04:04,460
Ögedei Kha'an
has shown me his mercy!

54
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:07,000
Let us all praise
his noble benevolence!

55
00:04:07,130 --> 00:04:09,300
[ALL] Huzzah!

56
00:04:09,630 --> 00:04:11,420
Huzzah!

57
00:04:11,550 --> 00:04:14,180
-Huh? What is all this?
- Huzzah!

58
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:19,100
-Huh?
-I now take my leave.

59
00:04:23,350 --> 00:04:26,230
I swear,
why did Chagatai do all that?

60
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:28,820
[CHINQAI] The prince put on
that performance for your sake.

61
00:04:29,320 --> 00:04:30,570
[ÖGEDEI] Chinqai?

62
00:04:32,110 --> 00:04:34,360
As one who only recently
took the throne,

63
00:04:34,490 --> 00:04:37,320
honor upon your name
is of the greatest importance.

64
00:04:37,450 --> 00:04:40,700
And what quality is prized most
among steppe tribe leaders?

65
00:04:40,830 --> 00:04:42,120
Benevolence?

66
00:04:42,330 --> 00:04:46,500
Exactly. Cruel to his foes,
and benevolent to his subjects.

67
00:04:46,630 --> 00:04:49,550
You've now proven yourself
to be precisely that.

68
00:04:49,670 --> 00:04:51,760
Well, I suppose it makes sense.

69
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:53,720
But why be so dramatic?

70
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:55,050
Huh?

71
00:04:56,470 --> 00:04:57,640
Now I understand.

72
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:00,260
-[birds screeching]
-Benevolence, indeed.

73
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:01,890
♪

74
00:05:02,770 --> 00:05:05,270
[SITARA (ADULT)] Kurultais were
held under Ögedei Kha'an

75
00:05:05,390 --> 00:05:08,770
to discuss matters
concerning future policies.

76
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:12,780
And in the Mongol Empire,
the emperor's consorts took part

77
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:14,860
in these political matters
as well.

78
00:05:15,610 --> 00:05:16,820
[Kirgistani grunts]

79
00:05:17,910 --> 00:05:19,120
Töregene?

80
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:21,830
What are you doing,
attending a Kurultai?

81
00:05:21,950 --> 00:05:23,330
You're hardly ever at these.

82
00:05:23,450 --> 00:05:24,540
Am I not permitted?

83
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:27,540
Some would give anything
to be here but cannot.

84
00:05:27,670 --> 00:05:28,830
[MÖGE] Hmph!

85
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:31,000
[ÖGEDEI] Uh? [chuckles]

86
00:05:31,130 --> 00:05:33,170
[MÖGE] Uh? [chuckles]

87
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:34,340
♪

88
00:05:36,470 --> 00:05:38,470
-Listen, Uqai.
-My name's Otai.

89
00:05:38,590 --> 00:05:40,390
Please try to remember that,
dear Father.

90
00:05:40,510 --> 00:05:41,430
[TEMÜGE] Mm...

91
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:44,520
Today's meeting will outline
our next military campaign.

92
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:47,690
Soon, we'll head eastward
and target the Jin Dynasty.

93
00:05:47,810 --> 00:05:48,810
[OTAI] From what I've heard,

94
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:50,650
they're responsible
for abducting and killing

95
00:05:50,770 --> 00:05:52,320
many of our forefathers.

96
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:54,940
Yes, but that's frankly
of little consequence

97
00:05:55,070 --> 00:05:56,110
at this point.

98
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,490
House Tolui
has the largest army.

99
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:02,160
But House Chagatai
has the Kha'an's trust.

100
00:06:02,290 --> 00:06:05,700
The head of House Jochi is dead
and his territory's far away.

101
00:06:05,830 --> 00:06:07,750
Whereas the lands of my House
of Temüge

102
00:06:07,870 --> 00:06:09,500
are close to the Jin's domain.

103
00:06:09,630 --> 00:06:10,790
Because our houses rule

104
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:13,210
over quite a large number
of subjects as of now,

105
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:16,340
we all want roles for ourselves
that won't incur losses.

106
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:18,720
So I'm wondering
how the new Kha'an

107
00:06:18,840 --> 00:06:20,640
will attempt to appease
each one of us.

108
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:21,970
Thoughts. Daritai?

109
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,510
Otai, Father.

110
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:25,430
[all murmuring]

111
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:26,850
Yes, true.

112
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:31,360
How will you handle
such an important matter,

113
00:06:31,900 --> 00:06:33,480
Great Kha'an?

114
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,530
[Ögedei inhales]

115
00:06:39,820 --> 00:06:42,030
I wish to build a great capital.

116
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,280
[ALL] Huh?

117
00:06:43,410 --> 00:06:44,540
[CHAGATAI] Uh-oh.

118
00:06:44,660 --> 00:06:47,080
[all gasp]

119
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,710
A capital, huh?

120
00:06:48,830 --> 00:06:50,750
Indeed, a capital.

121
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:53,090
We will construct a city
in the steppe.

122
00:06:53,210 --> 00:06:55,710
One made of permanent buildings,
rather than our tents.

123
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:58,220
Ah! What are you going on about?

124
00:06:58,340 --> 00:07:00,470
What of the campaign
to bring down the Jin?

125
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:01,930
A capital, you say?

126
00:07:02,050 --> 00:07:03,640
Do we all have to live there?

127
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:05,930
[VASSAL 1] We Mongols
take pride in crossing mountains

128
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:07,430
in pursuit of unseen lands.

129
00:07:07,560 --> 00:07:09,600
[VASSAL 2] Live like
settled people? Disgusting.

130
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:13,650
Everyone, the Great Kha'an
hasn't finished speaking yet.

131
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:17,530
[ÖGEDEI] It will be a capital,
but not one for us to live in.

132
00:07:17,650 --> 00:07:19,190
Workshops will be provided there

133
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:21,240
for crafting weapons
and jewelry.

134
00:07:21,360 --> 00:07:23,280
It will also serve
as a trading post

135
00:07:23,410 --> 00:07:24,740
where merchants can gather.

136
00:07:24,870 --> 00:07:27,870
We will all continue
our nomadic lifestyles.

137
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,460
But at times,
we will visit and spend freely.

138
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:33,750
In a show of our grace
and benevolence.

139
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:35,800
When word spreads
of such a place,

140
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:37,590
it's sure to attract
people and goods

141
00:07:37,710 --> 00:07:39,010
from across the land.

142
00:07:39,130 --> 00:07:40,300
What say you?

143
00:07:40,670 --> 00:07:42,510
This doesn't make
any sense at all.

144
00:07:42,630 --> 00:07:44,430
[all murmuring]

145
00:07:44,550 --> 00:07:46,810
[exhales] Will it not work?

146
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:49,640
Hmm...

147
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:51,480
[TOLUI] Sounds great to me!

148
00:07:53,270 --> 00:07:54,690
♪

149
00:07:55,730 --> 00:07:59,030
It's quite a curious proposal,
and one worth doing.

150
00:07:59,150 --> 00:08:00,780
[chuckles] Tolui.

151
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:03,030
Tell me, Great Kha'an.

152
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:09,290
When will we all
discuss the matter of war?

153
00:08:09,410 --> 00:08:10,700
[ÖGEDEI] Uh?

154
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:12,580
[Kirgistani grunts] Huh?

155
00:08:13,210 --> 00:08:17,630
Now the time is ripe to destroy
our sworn foes, the Jin.

156
00:08:18,630 --> 00:08:20,460
[TOLUI] Their formerly
vast territory has shrunk,

157
00:08:20,590 --> 00:08:22,550
so they're cornered
like tiny rats.

158
00:08:22,670 --> 00:08:25,970
And dealing the last blow
will be our Great Kha'an!

159
00:08:26,510 --> 00:08:27,510
[Ögedei chuckles]

160
00:08:28,510 --> 00:08:30,270
[TOLUI] This war will be just
like a circle hunt.

161
00:08:30,390 --> 00:08:33,190
Our quarry...
The Jin capital, Kaifeng.

162
00:08:33,310 --> 00:08:36,230
The Great Kha'an will set up
camp across the Yellow River,

163
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:37,940
directly to the north of it.

164
00:08:38,070 --> 00:08:40,110
While the rats tremble in fear,

165
00:08:40,230 --> 00:08:41,820
we'll pincer them
from the south.

166
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:45,490
That sounds more like hunting
deer than rats, if you ask me.

167
00:08:45,610 --> 00:08:47,530
Call them fawns if you prefer.

168
00:08:47,660 --> 00:08:50,200
Tolui, you mustn't
underestimate them.

169
00:08:50,330 --> 00:08:51,620
Though on the verge of collapse,

170
00:08:51,750 --> 00:08:54,580
the Jin vastly outnumber us
in both soldiers and subjects.

171
00:08:54,710 --> 00:08:55,790
[Tolui laughs]

172
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:57,790
Which is why I want you
to begin attacking

173
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:00,210
from the east and have
their citizens running, Uncle.

174
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:01,340
[TEMÜGE] Hmm?

175
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:03,220
[TOLUI] Just like you would
coax animals

176
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:04,760
into a hunting circle.

177
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:06,840
If we can chase the rest
of the Jin populace

178
00:09:06,970 --> 00:09:08,800
inside Kaifeng's walls,

179
00:09:09,050 --> 00:09:11,260
all those soldiers and subjects
you mentioned

180
00:09:11,390 --> 00:09:14,390
will be trapped in a city
that's completely closed off.

181
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:16,980
After winter passes
and all their food runs out,

182
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:19,610
I wonder what state
their poor town will be in.

183
00:09:19,730 --> 00:09:21,860
[laughs]

184
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:23,320
[Chagatai clears throat]

185
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:25,990
Oh, uh, as for you, brother...

186
00:09:26,110 --> 00:09:28,950
I think it's best if you
stay here and look after things.

187
00:09:29,070 --> 00:09:31,160
We should leave
our precious homeland

188
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:34,410
to the one the Great Kha'an
trusts more than anyone, right?

189
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:35,410
[ÖGEDEI] Hm.

190
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:37,580
Well, that's fine.

191
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:38,790
♪

192
00:09:40,630 --> 00:09:43,590
Jochi's kin will not have a part
to play here, I'm afraid.

193
00:09:43,710 --> 00:09:44,800
[ORDA] Huh?

194
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:47,840
In exchange for this,

195
00:09:47,970 --> 00:09:50,720
you will be leading some of our
other campaigns to the west.

196
00:09:50,850 --> 00:09:52,350
[ORDA] Mm...

197
00:09:52,510 --> 00:09:54,270
[TOLUI] How does that sound?

198
00:09:54,390 --> 00:09:56,890
Are any of you unhappy
with these war plans?

199
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,230
-[CHINQAI] Prince Tolui.
-Huh?

200
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:03,820
In order to approach Kaifeng
from the south,

201
00:10:03,940 --> 00:10:07,240
our warriors will be forced
into Southern Song territory.

202
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:09,700
And through precipitous
mountain roads at that.

203
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:11,280
It won't be a problem.

204
00:10:11,410 --> 00:10:13,740
The Southern Song are enemies
of the Jin, too,

205
00:10:13,870 --> 00:10:15,540
which makes them a friend to us.

206
00:10:15,660 --> 00:10:18,660
Now as for
the precipitous mountains...

207
00:10:19,170 --> 00:10:20,920
we'll prevail.

208
00:10:25,260 --> 00:10:28,050
[TÖREGENE] That's everything
they discussed at the Kurultai.

209
00:10:28,550 --> 00:10:30,390
Thank you very much.

210
00:10:31,260 --> 00:10:33,970
If Tolui's plans
eventually succeed,

211
00:10:34,100 --> 00:10:37,310
starvation and cold will await
the people of Kaifeng.

212
00:10:37,430 --> 00:10:39,810
I'm confronted
with this knowledge,

213
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:40,850
yet I still...

214
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:42,320
-[breathes shakily]
-Sitara,

215
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:44,400
do you feel unwell?
You're trembling.

216
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:45,650
[Sitara gasps]

217
00:10:46,030 --> 00:10:48,570
[stutters] I'm all right.
My apologies.

218
00:10:49,900 --> 00:10:51,490
Sitara...

219
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:55,620
Lady Töregene,

220
00:10:55,740 --> 00:10:58,750
I would prefer it
if you called me Fatima, please.

221
00:10:58,870 --> 00:11:00,000
Fatima?

222
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:03,590
Sitara is my name
from when I was a slave.

223
00:11:04,170 --> 00:11:06,300
It'd be improper
for somebody of low birth

224
00:11:06,420 --> 00:11:08,840
to serve the
Great Kha'an's consort.

225
00:11:09,170 --> 00:11:10,340
[Töregene sighs]

226
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:14,010
I, too, pass myself off
as a Naiman here.

227
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:15,220
[SITARA] Uh?

228
00:11:15,350 --> 00:11:17,270
[TÖREGENE]
After marrying a Merkit man,

229
00:11:17,390 --> 00:11:19,480
I would naturally
call myself one as well.

230
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:21,190
But there are
quite a few Mongols

231
00:11:21,310 --> 00:11:23,020
who don't take kindly to them.

232
00:11:23,730 --> 00:11:26,570
That's why I chose
to hide my past,

233
00:11:26,690 --> 00:11:29,320
and kept it a secret
from everyone I could.

234
00:11:29,450 --> 00:11:30,740
[Sitara gasps]

235
00:11:31,530 --> 00:11:34,410
Please keep it
a secret, too, Fatima.

236
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:35,830
[SITARA] I will.

237
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:39,660
She has the scent
of danger about her.

238
00:11:39,790 --> 00:11:42,330
So then, where do we go
from here?

239
00:11:42,460 --> 00:11:44,670
First, there is indeed
a power imbalance

240
00:11:44,790 --> 00:11:47,170
between the Great Kha'an
and Tolui family.

241
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:50,470
The House of Tolui commands
the largest Mongol army.

242
00:11:50,590 --> 00:11:52,180
The Great Kha'an has authority.

243
00:11:52,630 --> 00:11:55,180
And the House of Chagatai
supports him.

244
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:57,510
We must cause a rift
between them.

245
00:11:57,930 --> 00:11:59,390
But in order to do that,

246
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:01,480
Prince Tolui's big plan

247
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:03,600
will need to go off
successfully.

248
00:12:04,060 --> 00:12:05,110
♪

249
00:12:05,230 --> 00:12:06,650
[Boraqchin coughs]

250
00:12:08,820 --> 00:12:10,820
[MÖGE] Pardon the intrusion.

251
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:12,570
[chuckles]

252
00:12:14,070 --> 00:12:16,240
How are you feeling, Boraqchin?

253
00:12:17,990 --> 00:12:19,290
Well, seeing your face

254
00:12:19,410 --> 00:12:20,950
has certainly
brightened my mood a little.

255
00:12:21,910 --> 00:12:23,420
What do you have there?

256
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:24,670
This is a medical text

257
00:12:24,790 --> 00:12:26,670
brought here
by Quanzhen Daoists.

258
00:12:26,790 --> 00:12:28,090
[MÖGE] Hmm...

259
00:12:28,210 --> 00:12:30,300
Just through the process
of living,

260
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:32,420
our bodies gradually lose
their qi,

261
00:12:32,550 --> 00:12:34,430
which leads
to maladies and death.

262
00:12:34,550 --> 00:12:35,890
But through a specific training,

263
00:12:36,010 --> 00:12:38,140
you can stop the flow
of qi entirely.

264
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:40,430
It appears
that is their technique

265
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:42,180
for achieving immortality.

266
00:12:42,480 --> 00:12:43,890
[Möge exhales]

267
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:45,560
Will those techniques return you

268
00:12:45,690 --> 00:12:47,690
to your former health,
Boraqchin?

269
00:12:47,820 --> 00:12:49,190
Möge.

270
00:12:49,730 --> 00:12:53,150
It's just that you are supposed
to be the one sitting

271
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:55,700
at the Great Kha'an's side
at Kurultais.

272
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:59,120
And we desperately need
your clever mind.

273
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,450
[BORAQCHIN] Hmm.

274
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,710
Worry not.

275
00:13:02,830 --> 00:13:05,040
Kurultais aren't the only way
to decide things.

276
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:06,330
[MÖGE] Huh?

277
00:13:06,460 --> 00:13:07,750
[BORAQCHIN]
What's most important is

278
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:10,380
to discreetly maneuver
all manner of affairs.

279
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:12,300
And now then,

280
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:15,090
tell me about everything
you have heard lately.

281
00:13:15,930 --> 00:13:17,140
[Möge chuckles]

282
00:13:17,970 --> 00:13:19,390
[SITARA] Prince Tolui's plan

283
00:13:19,510 --> 00:13:21,430
puts most of the burden
on himself.

284
00:13:21,560 --> 00:13:22,890
But should he succeed,

285
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:25,060
he will also earn
the most acclaim.

286
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:28,230
I believe he will
most likely succeed.

287
00:13:28,860 --> 00:13:30,770
After all, the House of Tolui

288
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:33,070
does have the strongest army
of the Mongols.

289
00:13:33,530 --> 00:13:36,780
The Mongol army typically
employs audacious tactics,

290
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:38,950
which will startle the enemy.

291
00:13:39,740 --> 00:13:40,780
However...

292
00:13:40,910 --> 00:13:43,910
However,
the other Mongol princes

293
00:13:44,040 --> 00:13:45,750
will reach the same conclusion.

294
00:13:45,870 --> 00:13:47,710
The House of Tolui...

295
00:13:47,830 --> 00:13:49,170
[BOTH]...is too powerful.

296
00:13:49,290 --> 00:13:50,460
[Möge gasps]

297
00:13:50,790 --> 00:13:54,340
Even if Tolui doesn't intend
to betray anyone,

298
00:13:54,470 --> 00:13:56,760
should the Houses begin
to fear his strength,

299
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:58,760
and harbor distrust
toward him...

300
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:01,010
and should they decide
to collude

301
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:03,100
against the House of Tolui,

302
00:14:03,390 --> 00:14:05,520
I am certain...

303
00:14:06,520 --> 00:14:08,140
[SITARA]
The Mongols will fracture.

304
00:14:08,270 --> 00:14:10,440
And eventually fall to ruin.

305
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:11,690
[BORAQCHIN] There will be those

306
00:14:11,820 --> 00:14:14,280
who aim to sow
the seeds of discord.

307
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:16,200
But then, what can we do?

308
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:17,490
Möge...

309
00:14:17,610 --> 00:14:20,490
You are still young
and beautiful, unlike me.

310
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:21,950
And honest and amiable.

311
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:23,280
[MÖGE] Uh...

312
00:14:23,910 --> 00:14:26,710
[BORAQCHIN] To ensure
the Mongols are not divided,

313
00:14:26,830 --> 00:14:29,500
and to ensure
our hearts remain as one,

314
00:14:29,630 --> 00:14:32,380
I need you to take steps
in my stead.

315
00:14:32,500 --> 00:14:33,630
[MÖGE] Hmm.

316
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:37,340
I'll do what you need
of me, Boraqchin.

317
00:14:37,470 --> 00:14:38,510
♪

318
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:42,720
[SITARA]
Driven into a closed-off city

319
00:14:42,850 --> 00:14:45,680
to ultimately perish
from hunger and cold.

320
00:14:45,810 --> 00:14:49,020
The people of Tus
could have met the same fate.

321
00:14:49,690 --> 00:14:52,060
To the citizens of Kaifeng,

322
00:14:52,190 --> 00:14:55,440
I'd be no different
than any other Mongol.

323
00:14:56,490 --> 00:14:57,820
♪

324
00:15:12,840 --> 00:15:14,920
The Great Kha'an
heads off to war,

325
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:17,590
and Prince Chagatai stays
to watch the steppe.

326
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:19,760
What shall we be doing
during this time?

327
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:22,300
[TÖREGENE] We will accompany
the Great Kha'an's army

328
00:15:22,430 --> 00:15:23,550
to the front-line camp.

329
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:26,010
Chagatai is here now
to say his farewells

330
00:15:26,140 --> 00:15:27,100
to the Great Kha'an.

331
00:15:27,220 --> 00:15:28,560
Once we depart,

332
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:31,520
we probably won't be seeing him
for quite a long time.

333
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:34,020
[SITARA] To cause turmoil
among the Mongols,

334
00:15:34,150 --> 00:15:36,780
we need a faction that will
oppose the House of Tolui.

335
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:39,570
The House of Chagatai is
an indispensable part of that.

336
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:43,160
Well then, please allow me
to go to him as your messenger,

337
00:15:43,280 --> 00:15:45,580
and give Prince Chagatai
our warmest regards.

338
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:48,370
I, Fatima,
am your humble servant.

339
00:15:53,710 --> 00:15:54,750
[QADAQ] Hmm?

340
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:56,840
[cattle mooing]

341
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:01,050
[hammering]

342
00:16:01,170 --> 00:16:03,590
[indistinct chatter]

343
00:16:09,730 --> 00:16:10,890
[horse neighs]

344
00:16:13,850 --> 00:16:16,690
Hold on. Why are you
following me, Sir Qadaq?

345
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:18,650
I can't let you go by yourself.

346
00:16:18,780 --> 00:16:20,740
Oh, I never took you
to be such a gentleman.

347
00:16:20,860 --> 00:16:23,070
No, I'm saying
I don't trust you.

348
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:25,870
Lady Töregene trusts me,
isn't that enough?

349
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:28,620
Well, she's not the one I serve.

350
00:16:28,740 --> 00:16:30,330
So it's a long story.

351
00:16:30,450 --> 00:16:32,790
But I'm actually acting
on someone else's ord...

352
00:16:32,910 --> 00:16:34,210
[gasps]

353
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:38,500
[gasps]

354
00:16:39,420 --> 00:16:40,670
[gasps]

355
00:16:43,090 --> 00:16:44,720
[Sitara pants]

356
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:49,310
[MÖGE] Hey! Aren't you
Töregene's slave?

357
00:16:49,430 --> 00:16:52,020
Yes, you there.
What are you doing out here?

358
00:16:52,140 --> 00:16:53,770
[Sitara gasps] This woman...

359
00:16:53,890 --> 00:16:56,860
is Lady Möge, the fourth wife
of the Great Kha'an!

360
00:16:56,980 --> 00:17:01,030
Oh. I see.
You just don't learn, do you?

361
00:17:01,570 --> 00:17:03,400
[Sitara gasps, whimpers]

362
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:06,280
Are you lost again?

363
00:17:06,410 --> 00:17:09,160
-Hm?
-You are lost, aren't you?

364
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:11,370
I know! I bet you're
still struggling

365
00:17:11,490 --> 00:17:13,290
to learn the locations
of all the tents in our camp.

366
00:17:13,410 --> 00:17:14,660
I've had my suspicions

367
00:17:14,790 --> 00:17:16,710
ever since you got caught
wandering around

368
00:17:16,830 --> 00:17:19,880
and Töregene had to make up
an excuse for you.

369
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,380
-Or maybe...
-Fine, you figured it out.

370
00:17:23,510 --> 00:17:25,380
-[cries]
-That's what I thought.

371
00:17:25,510 --> 00:17:26,890
-What should I do?
-Hmm.

372
00:17:27,010 --> 00:17:28,680
I'll bring shame
upon Lady Töregene

373
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:30,430
and be scolded again.

374
00:17:30,560 --> 00:17:32,720
It's no business of mine
if Töregene scolds you.

375
00:17:32,850 --> 00:17:35,730
But bringing shame to the
Great Kha'an is another thing.

376
00:17:35,850 --> 00:17:37,020
Allow me to show you the way.

377
00:17:37,310 --> 00:17:41,110
[exclaims] Really? I can't
thank you enough, Lady Möge.

378
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:43,320
I need to figure
a way out of this.

379
00:17:44,530 --> 00:17:47,530
Something about her
seems different than last time.

380
00:17:48,570 --> 00:17:50,780
-The earrings.
-[Möge gasps]

381
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:54,540
Uh... I'm so sorry.

382
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:58,000
Do I look odd without them?

383
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:01,590
Oh, no, I wouldn't say
you look "odd."

384
00:18:02,130 --> 00:18:04,300
-But...
-[Möge sighs]

385
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:07,430
[SITARA] Did you happen
to misplace them recently?

386
00:18:07,590 --> 00:18:08,800
[Möge grunts]

387
00:18:08,930 --> 00:18:10,010
No.

388
00:18:10,550 --> 00:18:12,890
The Great Kha'an chose
to sell them.

389
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:14,060
[POOR MAN] Great Kha'an!

390
00:18:14,430 --> 00:18:17,980
Oh, Great Kha'an, I beg of you
to buy this melon from me.

391
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:20,150
I am just ever so impoverished.

392
00:18:20,270 --> 00:18:21,770
It's so small.

393
00:18:21,900 --> 00:18:24,820
Möge, please give this man
those earrings you're wearing.

394
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:26,030
[MÖGE] What!

395
00:18:26,530 --> 00:18:29,780
[poor man exclaims]

396
00:18:29,910 --> 00:18:32,080
[laughs]

397
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:33,830
[ÖGEDEI] Worry not, Möge.

398
00:18:34,330 --> 00:18:36,330
I truly believe
that those earrings

399
00:18:36,450 --> 00:18:39,120
are destined to return
to you in the future.

400
00:18:39,670 --> 00:18:41,540
He said they'll return?

401
00:18:41,670 --> 00:18:43,090
What could he have meant
by that?

402
00:18:43,210 --> 00:18:44,460
I don't know in the least.

403
00:18:44,710 --> 00:18:47,340
I still cannot understand the
Great Kha'an in the slightest.

404
00:18:47,460 --> 00:18:48,840
-[CHINQAI] Lady Möge!
-Mm?

405
00:18:48,970 --> 00:18:51,680
Lady Möge,
the Great Kha'an calls for you.

406
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:53,310
What does he want?

407
00:18:53,430 --> 00:18:55,180
I wasn't informed
of the details.

408
00:18:55,310 --> 00:18:58,180
-[exhales] Chuu!
-[horse neighs]

409
00:18:59,350 --> 00:19:01,060
[ÖGEDEI]
It shouldn't be long now.

410
00:19:01,190 --> 00:19:02,310
[hooves clopping]

411
00:19:03,570 --> 00:19:04,860
Oh, there she is.

412
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:06,610
Greetings, Möge.

413
00:19:06,990 --> 00:19:08,440
Come sit here.

414
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:15,660
I have here a gift for you.

415
00:19:17,330 --> 00:19:18,410
[Möge gasps]

416
00:19:19,870 --> 00:19:21,250
[MÖGE] It can't be.

417
00:19:21,370 --> 00:19:22,750
[Sitara gasps]

418
00:19:24,590 --> 00:19:26,760
[Möge exclaiming]

419
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:29,300
But these are my earrings!

420
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:31,220
[ÖGEDEI] Where did you manage
to obtain these?

421
00:19:31,340 --> 00:19:33,850
That would be Khorasan.

422
00:19:33,970 --> 00:19:36,680
While I was on my journey
to Samarkand,

423
00:19:36,810 --> 00:19:39,560
I was fortunate enough
to meet a trader who told me

424
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:41,850
that he had some fine treasures
from the east.

425
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:43,940
Might I interest you in these?

426
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:48,280
I asked him where he ever
could have come across

427
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,990
such magnificent pearl earrings.

428
00:19:50,110 --> 00:19:52,740
He said that he found them
in a Uyghur city

429
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:54,700
by a random stroke of luck.

430
00:19:54,830 --> 00:19:55,990
-He received them...
-Please, sir.

431
00:19:56,280 --> 00:19:58,490
...from a poor man on the verge
of starving to death,

432
00:19:58,620 --> 00:20:01,250
in exchange
for a few loaves of bread.

433
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:03,920
So Khorasan, huh?

434
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:05,840
That's further than I expected.

435
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:08,250
I believe earrings
as splendid as these

436
00:20:08,380 --> 00:20:10,800
truly befit the grand conqueror
of the world.

437
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:12,880
That is why
I came here immediately

438
00:20:13,010 --> 00:20:16,260
to present them as an offering,
Great Kha'an.

439
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:20,730
[MÖGE]
They really did return to me.

440
00:20:20,850 --> 00:20:23,140
Thank you
for delivering them to me.

441
00:20:23,270 --> 00:20:24,980
I will buy all of your goods,

442
00:20:25,110 --> 00:20:26,570
and your fellow merchants'
as well.

443
00:20:26,690 --> 00:20:28,730
[exclaims] Thank you very much.

444
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:29,940
All of them?

445
00:20:30,070 --> 00:20:32,740
Bring me more of your wares
in the future.

446
00:20:32,860 --> 00:20:34,530
You will not regret it.

447
00:20:39,450 --> 00:20:40,660
[CHINQAI] Uh...

448
00:20:41,330 --> 00:20:43,580
Uh... Ah, over there will do.

449
00:20:43,710 --> 00:20:45,330
Just put them
with all the others.

450
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:46,920
Be careful handling that.

451
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:49,630
[TRADER 1] I didn't expect him
to buy everything from us.

452
00:20:49,750 --> 00:20:52,630
Coming to Mongolia
was the right decision.

453
00:20:52,760 --> 00:20:53,840
[SITARA] Excuse me.

454
00:20:53,970 --> 00:20:55,300
[TRADERS] Hmm?

455
00:20:55,430 --> 00:20:58,600
My apologies.
You traveled here from Khorasan?

456
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:00,310
[ABD] We did. Who are you?

457
00:21:00,430 --> 00:21:02,890
I originally hail
from Khorasan as well.

458
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:05,600
Why have you made your way
all the way to Mongolia?

459
00:21:05,730 --> 00:21:07,190
You're asking why?

460
00:21:07,310 --> 00:21:09,940
It is simple.
Because Mongolia is where

461
00:21:10,070 --> 00:21:12,030
the most profit
is to be had, of course.

462
00:21:12,150 --> 00:21:14,280
We had figured that
the Mongol emperor would be

463
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:17,070
more likely than most
to offer high prices for wares

464
00:21:17,200 --> 00:21:19,160
coming from Khorasan
and points west.

465
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:21,790
But weren't you afraid
to come here?

466
00:21:21,910 --> 00:21:23,910
The journey is a long one,

467
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:26,290
and the Mongols
are a frightening people.

468
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:29,750
Not at all. In fact, it is safer
to travel now than before.

469
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:31,090
[Sitara gasps]

470
00:21:31,420 --> 00:21:34,380
The Mongols appoint officials to
govern the lands they conquer.

471
00:21:34,510 --> 00:21:37,720
Their duty is to protect
merchants passing through them.

472
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:40,850
[TRADER] The emperor is
a remarkable man, indeed.

473
00:21:40,970 --> 00:21:43,270
[ÖGEDEI]
Thanks to your lovely earrings,

474
00:21:43,390 --> 00:21:46,350
I have learned that
all is functioning as it should.

475
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:47,810
♪

476
00:21:52,860 --> 00:21:54,780
[ÖGEDEI]
I have to wonder, though.

477
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:57,400
Will people come
to see it my way

478
00:21:57,530 --> 00:21:59,830
after we have defeated
all the Jin?

479
00:22:02,830 --> 00:22:05,200
[♪ closing theme song playing]

480
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:36,260
[SITARA (ADULT)] Next time,
"Great Khatun Boraqchin."

